course: dictionary
lesson: 15672
title: Thumbnail: a nail, a picture, a short sketch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Thumbnail is a good example. «She cut her thumbnail on the sharp lid.» Here the clue is thumb: a thumbnail is the nail on your thumb.
explain: «I clicked the thumbnail and the video started.» On a screen, a thumbnail is a small picture that stands for a bigger picture or video. The clues are clicked and video: you click it to see the full one.
explain: «The artist drew a thumbnail sketch before painting the castle.» Thumbnail can also describe something, so it is an adjective. A thumbnail sketch or description is very short and gives only the main points. The clue is sketch: a quick plan, not a finished picture.
fact: A thumbnail is the nail on your thumb.
fact: On a screen, a thumbnail is a small picture that stands for a bigger picture or video.
fact: A thumbnail sketch or description is very short and gives only the main points.
fact: Some video thumbnails are made to look exciting to trick you into clicking; this is called «clickbait».
fact: Artists often do a thumbnail sketch to plan a picture before they paint it.
exercise: «She cut her thumbnail on the sharp lid.» What is a thumbnail in this sentence? | *The nail on your thumb | A kind of glove | A small picture on a screen | A very short description
exercise: «I clicked the thumbnail and the video started.» What does thumbnail mean here? | A short written summary of a book | A loud sound from the speakers | The nail on your thumb | *A small picture that stands for a bigger one
exercise: «The artist drew a thumbnail sketch before painting the castle.» What is a thumbnail sketch? | A sketch drawn with a thumb only | A photo taken on a phone | *A small, quick plan showing the main shapes | A huge painting in full colour
test: «The thumbnail showed a smiling dog, but the video was about boring homework.» Why might a thumbnail be misleading? | *It may have been made to look exciting, to trick you into clicking | It is the nail of the person who made the video | It is always a true copy of the next scene | It always shows the whole video in tiny size
test: «Her thumbnail biography of Marie Curie gave only the key facts.» What does thumbnail mean here? | Very long and full of detail | *Very short, giving only the main points | Written with a thumb on a phone | About a person's hands
exam: «The thumbnail on the screen was tiny, but the picture behind it was huge.» What is the thumbnail? | A huge poster on the wall | *A small picture that stands for a bigger one | The nail on your hand | A long story about a famous person
